// Robust COGO Test Script - Reverse Curves Feature
// This script specifically evaluates compounding and reverse
// tangential curves branching off the same alignment string.

CLEAR
LOG ON

// ==========================================
// 1. Establish Control Backbone
// ==========================================
// We'll map out a straight "street" to use as our tangent spine.
NE 1 5000.0000 5000.0000 "Start of Street"
NE 2 6000.0000 5000.0000 "PI 1"
NE 3 7000.0000 5000.0000 "PI 2"
NE 4 8000.0000 5000.0000 "End of Street"

// ==========================================
// 2. Build S-Curve (Reverse Curve)
// ==========================================
BEG S_CURVE_TEST
FIG 1
FIG 2

// Curve Right (Eastward turn if moving North)
// Bulging Right:
XC BD (BULB)  250.0 1 45.0000 100.0
XC BD (BULB)  250.0 1 70.0000 100.0
XC BD (BULB)  250.0 1 90.0000 100.0

// Reverse Curve! Inflection Point.
// Curve Left (Bulging back towards center-line / Westward)
XC BD (BULB) -250.0 1 110.0000 100.0
XC BD (BULB) -250.0 1 135.0000 100.0
XC BD (BULB) -250.0 1 160.0000 100.0

FIG 3
FIG 4

// Standard looping back to Origin to allow MAPCHECK closure.
NE 5 8000.0000 4000.0000 "Return Frame"
NE 6 5000.0000 4000.0000 "Return Frame"
FIG 5
FIG 6
FIG 1
END

// Validate the Figure Closure traversing through the Reverse Curve
MAPCHECK S_CURVE_TEST

// ==========================================
// 3. Nested Serpentine Curves
// ==========================================
// Creates a tight serpentine pattern bounded explicitly 
BEG SERPENTINE_WALK
NE 100 4000.0000 4000.0000 "Walk Start"
FIG 100
// Serpentine 1
XC ZD (BULB) 50.0 0.0000 25.0
XC ZD (BULB) 50.0 30.0000 25.0
// Reverse 1
XC ZD (BULB) -50.0 60.0000 25.0
XC ZD (BULB) -50.0 90.0000 25.0
// Reverse 2
XC ZD (BULB) 50.0 120.0000 25.0
XC ZD (BULB) 50.0 150.0000 25.0
// Reverse 3
XC ZD (BULB) -50.0 180.0000 25.0
XC ZD (BULB) -50.0 210.0000 25.0
END

LIST PTS
SAVE reverse_curves_test.cogo
LOG OFF
